<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Average Noise Reduction - Polylines</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal; font-weight:bold;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Polylines &gt; Reduce Noise &gt; Average</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>.</b></span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description: &#160;</b></span></b><span class="Command">verage Noise Reduction</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command reduces noise in the visible selected polylines by applying an average (Laplacian) filter. Co-ordinates of every point are based on the average of co-ordinates of its neighbouring points. In contrast to the Average filter for scan data and meshes, curvature is not taking into account. All points in the data will be modified, including critical features.</span></p>
<p class="Normal"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image002.jpg" width="302px" height="196px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Strength</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Specifies how strong the filter to be applied, i.e. number of iterations. It ranges from 1 to 10. Default strength for this command is 1. Using a low strength setting will mean that only small changes will be made to the selection. Increasing the strength setting will result in smoother polylines with larger changes.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is grayed if there is no selection or all selections are hidden. It works on wholly selected polylines as well as on partial selections.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP165484873" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table cellspacing="5" class="whs5">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs6">
<td class="whs7">
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image006.jpg" width="301px" height="196px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs9">
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image008.jpg" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs6">
<td class="whs11">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Polyline before applying Average filter</span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs12">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Polyline after applying Average filter</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Poor surface finish, direct reflections or using incorrect laser power setting may cause noise in the data, which later reflects to the polylines.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span> <span class="Command">Average Noise Reduction</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to remove any small imperfections in the isolated polyline fragments.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>See also</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span> <u style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="Median_Noise_Reduction_-_Polylines.htm">Median Noise Reduction</a></span></u></p>
